Files in this folder are Skia (<https://skia.org>), as LiveCode's
livecode-thirdparty carried it: the sources of revision 20471894
(git-revision.txt), with what LiveCode's gyp build compiles
(libskia.gyp).

One local change, marked "OXT-Beyond" in the source:

- In include/private/SkFixed.h, SkFixedMul_arm, which 32-bit ARM builds
  use for SkFixedMul, returns the portable product (SkFixedMul_longlong)
  where it had inline assembly (smull, then two instructions putting
  bits 16 to 47 of the 64-bit product together): the same result for
  every input, and what upstream Skia uses on ARM since. The assembly's
  operands let Clang give the product's two halves one register, which
  the ARM architecture leaves unpredictable and Clang's integrated
  assembler, the only assembler in an Android NDK from r24 on, refuses.
  tools/ci/tests/test_android_engine.py compares the two products.
